---
import HaldenImage from "./HaldenImage.astro";
---

<section id="materials" class="bleed-section bg-base-100" aria-labelledby="materials-heading">
  <div class="container-halden bleed-section__grid">
    <div class="bleed-section__media bleed-section__media--left bleed-left scroll-reveal">
      <HaldenImage
        base="/images/materials"
        alt="Gold-fill chain and sterling wire photographed on a work surface."
        width={1500}
        height={1000}
        comment="Materials: gold-fill chain and sterling wire"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="bleed-section__copy bleed-section__copy--right scroll-reveal">
      <div class="section-header">
        <p class="text-eyebrow">Materials</p>
        <h2 id="materials-heading" class="text-headline-sm">
          Gold-fill, not gold-plated.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="text-body mt-48 max-w-none md:mt-64">
        Plating is measured in microns and wears through in a year. Gold-fill is
        a bonded layer roughly a hundred times thicker, and it does not wear off.
        Everything else is .925 sterling, oxidised by hand. Freshwater pearls
        come from one supplier in Vancouver. There is no nickel in anything we
        make.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
